{% doc %}
  The class list for a section container.

  ## Where the width comes from

  A section passes its own setting. When that setting is empty — a section added
  before the setting existed, or one that deliberately has no control — the
  theme's **Layout width** is used instead, so a store has one place to set its
  overall proportions and sections only override where they need to.

  ## The five widths

    edge      Runs to the screen edge, keeping only the gutter.
    wide      1700px.
    standard  1440px. The default.
    compact   1100px.
    custom    Whatever **Custom width** is set to in theme settings.

  Compact, Standard and Wide are constants in `assets/base.css` rather than
  three sliders, because three independent sliders can be put in the wrong order
  — Wide narrower than Standard — and then every section using them disagrees
  with its own label. Custom is the escape hatch, and it is a single shared
  value: a section chooses *whether* to use it, not what it is. That is why the
  section panel has no slider of its own.

  ## Unrecognised values fall back rather than break

  A stored value from an older schema resolves to the theme's layout width, not
  to a class that does not exist.

  Parameters:
    width   (string)  edge | wide | standard | compact | custom.
                      Falls back to `settings.layout_width`.
    classes (string)  Extra classes to append.

  @example
    <div class="{% render 'container', width: section.settings.container_width %}">

  @example
    <div class="{% render 'container', classes: 'header__inner' %}">
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign resolved = width | default: settings.layout_width | default: 'standard'

  case resolved
    when 'edge'
      assign width_class = 'container container--edge'
    when 'wide'
      assign width_class = 'container container--wide'
    when 'compact'
      assign width_class = 'container container--compact'
    when 'custom'
      assign width_class = 'container container--custom'
    when 'flush'
      assign width_class = 'container container--flush'
    else
      assign width_class = 'container container--standard'
  endcase

  assign out = width_class
  if classes != blank
    assign out = out | append: ' ' | append: classes
  endif
-%}
{{- out -}}
